  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kentucky has recorded $92M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state received 505 awards with an average award size of $182K. Obligations fell 99.0% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a sharp drop from prior years: FY22 was $12.3B, FY23 was $13B, FY24 was $12.9B, FY25 was $10.8B, and FY26 was $9.5B. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $40.1M in Kentucky this fiscal year to date, and the Department of the Treasury obligated $36.4M. WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC received $36M in obligations and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying is the largest industry by obligations at $36M. Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools accounted for $7.9M in obligations, and Universities such as UNIVERSITY OF LOUISVILLE and UNIVERSITY OF KENTUCKY received $7.5M and $4.6M respectively. The FY2027 totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and reflect obligations recorded so far this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in Kentucky federal contracting this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.0% year over year. Total obligations for FY2027 to date are $92M, down from $9.5B in FY26 and from higher totals in FY22 through FY25. Award activity shows 505 awards with an average award size of $182K, reflecting the current fiscal year to date picture. The FY2027 totals are partial and represent obligations recorded so far."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and contractors in Kentucky this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $40.1M and the Department of the Treasury obligated $36.4M in Kentucky for FY2027 to date. WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC received $36M, and UNIVERSITY OF LOUISVILLE received $7.5M. Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying is the top industry at $36M, and Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools accounted for $7.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
