      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Kentucky?",
      "a": "Kentucky received $92M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Total obligations for prior fiscal years were $12.3B in FY22, $13B in FY23, $12.9B in FY24, $10.8B in FY25, and $9.5B in FY26, and the FY2027 figure is partial, fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Kentucky?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of the Treasury are the largest buyers in Kentucky for FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $40.1M and the Department of the Treasury obligated $36.4M, followed by the Department of Justice at $13.6M and the Department of Agriculture at $2.2M."
    },
